nberg SFB, CA Jobs Virginia Beach, VA Jobs WA, Joint Base Lewis- McChord (JBLM) Jobs Waldorf, MD Jobs Washington DC Jobs Advanced Job Search Talent Network UMGC offers the prestige of being part of the acclaimed University System of Maryland as well as a flexible schedule that fits your life. Teaching highly motivated, working adult students in more than 95 different programs, our adjunct/faculty and collegiate faculty have the freedom to work online from most locations in the world — or on-site at one of more than 100 classroom locations, both within the United States and abroad. Some classes even utilize a hybrid format with face-to-face and online learning, leveraging both formats to offer the best of both worlds. Bring your real-world experience. Here you’ll find the opportunity to collaborate with other professionals from diverse backgrounds – ranging from academia to military officers and corporate executives – bringing real-world experience to our curriculum, and providing our students with the practical skills and knowledge to improve their lives for the better. We're Here for You Adjunct Faculty Our adjunct faculty teach a maximum of 18 credits per academic year, either online, on-site or in hybrid courses at our many locations across Maryland, Northern Virginia and Washington, D.C. Collegiate Faculty In addition to adjunct/faculty positions, UMGC occasionally has collegiate/faculty positions, which include such administrative roles as Academic Directors and Program Directors. Why Choose UMGC? Flexible Scheduling Strong Academic Reputation More Than 95 Online Degree and Certificate Programs Innovative Technologies Comprehensive Faculty Development Program Faculty Awards Programs Excellent Benefits Recognized worldwide as a pioneer in online education, UMGC is more than a great place to learn – it’s an extraordinary place to work. UMGC Careers. Never Stop Learning. Join Our Talent Community Stay connected with UMGC and receive alerts with new job opportunities and news relative to your interests Sign Up Now All external hires will be subject to the satisfactory completion of a pre-employment background review. This includes, but is not limited to, employment and education verification and criminal records check. Certain designated jobs are subject to a pre-employment assessment. We are an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer. Annual Safety and Security Report (opens in a new window) © University of Maryland Global Campus. All rights reserved. Mailing Address No classes or services at this location 3501 University Blvd. East, Adelphi, MD   20783 Get Social (opens in a new window)"
